illumos port of libglnx (FreeBSD's fork arrowd/libglnx at c210033e, which
the component unpacks into subprojects/libglnx, as FreeBSD's port does):
- its raw Linux system calls (statx, openat2, open_tree, renameat2, ...)
  fail with ENOSYS instead of raising SIGSYS with unknown numbers;
- no O_TMPFILE fallback bit (it means something else on illumos), an
  AT_EMPTY_PATH value no illumos flag uses, no O_PATH (open for reading);
- no FICLONE ioctl, no sendfile() (read/write is used), TIOCGWINSZ from
  <sys/termios.h>, no Linux fstatfs() automount check;
- struct dirent has no d_type: new glnx_dirent_is_dir() for the callers.

Not upstream yet; meant for https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libglnx

